<title>ITALY: Italy 6-14 trln lire short of 3-pct EMU goal - Prodi.</title>
<headline>Italy 6-14 trln lire short of 3-pct EMU goal - Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Romano Prodi said on Friday that Italy was currently some six to 14 trillion lire ($3.6-$8.4 billion) short of the Maastricht goal of a deficit that is three percent of gross domestic product (GDP).</p>
<p>Prodi said in a speech to a congress of the Democratic Party of the Left (PDS), the biggest in his centre-left government, that the 1998 budget would be worth 0.5 percent of GDP if the mini-budget he announced earlier this week is carried out.</p>
</text>
